# Settings of the phone (docs/remote.md). They change nothing on the VPS, which has a .env of its own: a brief
# asked for with a button is made on the VPS, with the VPS's settings.
#
# setup.sh copies this to .env at the repo root (git-ignored). Unset, a setting has the value shown.

# The VPS, as named in ~/.ssh/config.
#XMD_VPS_HOST=xmd-vps

# Where a brief ends up: one made on the VPS is downloaded there, one made on the phone is copied there. Any folder
# the Files app can see, or one inside your vault.
#XMD_BRIEF_DEST="$HOME/storage/shared/Documents/xmd-briefs"

# A brief made on the phone itself also needs the model's settings: `bash deploy/termux/setup.sh alone` adds them
# below, from deploy/env.example.
